<node id="Docker">
  <data key="d0">Docker</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Docker is a versatile platform designed for the development, deployment, and distribution of applications within containers. It allows developers to encapsulate applications in isolated environments, ensuring that the application runs consistently across different computing environments. The platform is widely used for containerization, which is the process of packaging an application with all its dependencies into a single unit, known as a container. This enables applications to be deployed quickly and reliably, as the containers are portable and self-contained. Docker supports the LightRAG system, a technology that can be deployed on the platform. Additionally, Docker facilitates the shipping and running of containerized applications, making it a comprehensive solution for the lifecycle of applications from development to distribution.&lt;SEP&gt;A software container platform</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8b9291b4c9b5aad9fbc21176a5512b06-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8b9291b4c9b5aad9fbc21176a5512b06-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1df1634555d20a3b0378d0dc58979df0-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8b4d4a34c28646786713dd9d097373d4-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-497eef1a84c2e1267fe9ef217a5f0106-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a1c50a7f3809140ca9c7d7176ff5b4ed-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5ce3beac28f955cae00646a6f9e69a70-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5ce3beac28f955cae00646a6f9e69a70-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1c9ad9caff9f78bc752ac6a5d55c8af6-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786009855</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
