<node id=".env">
  <data key="d0">.env</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The `.env` file is a configuration file utilized primarily for storing and managing environment variables. It is employed in various contexts to configure systems, such as the LightRAG system, by holding configuration parameters. Specifically, the `.env` file is considered the main environment variable file for the LightRAG Server, from which the server loads its settings. It serves as a means to store and retrieve environment variables that are crucial for configuring a service, providing a structured and centralized approach to handling configuration data within the LightRAG Server project.&lt;SEP&gt;A file containing environment variables for the LightRAG system</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8b9291b4c9b5aad9fbc21176a5512b06-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8b9291b4c9b5aad9fbc21176a5512b06-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1df1634555d20a3b0378d0dc58979df0-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1df1634555d20a3b0378d0dc58979df0-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8b4d4a34c28646786713dd9d097373d4-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8b4d4a34c28646786713dd9d097373d4-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-497eef1a84c2e1267fe9ef217a5f0106-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-497eef1a84c2e1267fe9ef217a5f0106-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a583d83915dae1536924c9149ccfaa0-chunk-004</data>
