  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="chunk_options">
  <data key="d0">chunk_options</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The chunk_options represent a data element that encapsulates the various chunking parameters and strategies for a given strategy. This component is instrumental in determining which parameters the chunker employs, and it includes the strategy sub-dictionary selected by the `process_options`. The field serves as a frozen snapshot of the chunker parameters at the time of enqueue, deciding which chunking strategy to utilize. Specifically, chunk_options encompass the choices for chunking documents, which are applicable within the LightRAG Server. Each document has a unique snapshot of the chunk options stored, forming a set of chunking options that define how the data is divided and processed.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1df1634555d20a3b0378d0dc58979df0-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1df1634555d20a3b0378d0dc58979df0-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1df1634555d20a3b0378d0dc58979df0-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1df1634555d20a3b0378d0dc58979df0-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1df1634555d20a3b0378d0dc58979df0-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-497eef1a84c2e1267fe9ef217a5f0106-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-497eef1a84c2e1267fe9ef217a5f0106-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-832e2be61d469cc5f7dd74904c81d721-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786008621</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
