<node id="content">
  <data key="d0">content</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The entity "content" refers to the textual information that is processed or stored within various contexts. It encompasses the main text content of a document, including but not limited to body text under headings, and can also include additional elements such as equations, images, and tables. The content field can be extracted from raw parse formats and may be empty or pending in certain states, while in a lightrag state, it represents the complete merged text. Internally, temporary fields may be used for splitting and merging content. This content can be part of a chunk or a block within a document, serving as the textual foundation for various document components.&lt;SEP&gt;The main body of a document</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1df1634555d20a3b0378d0dc58979df0-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1df1634555d20a3b0378d0dc58979df0-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d37ce0e26a92a51f4827fa69633d38eb-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d37ce0e26a92a51f4827fa69633d38eb-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d37ce0e26a92a51f4827fa69633d38eb-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d37ce0e26a92a51f4827fa69633d38eb-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-832e2be61d469cc5f7dd74904c81d721-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-832e2be61d469cc5f7dd74904c81d721-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-832e2be61d469cc5f7dd74904c81d721-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e19e78061b434feb53d27d2650de9433-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786010519</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
