<node id="doc_id">
  <data key="d0">doc_id</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The `doc_id` is a unique identifier for a document, serving as a globally unique identifier in the format `doc-&lt;md5&gt;`. It is used to identify a specific document within the full_docs structure and represents a physical or digital object created by humans. The `doc_id` can also be referred to as a custom document ID, and it is simply an identifier for a document.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1df1634555d20a3b0378d0dc58979df0-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1df1634555d20a3b0378d0dc58979df0-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d37ce0e26a92a51f4827fa69633d38eb-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-832e2be61d469cc5f7dd74904c81d721-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-832e2be61d469cc5f7dd74904c81d721-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-832e2be61d469cc5f7dd74904c81d721-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c23c1da1b37f05359c98c1d67e825dee-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3a7e545539453c5dfacd0828fae0fc39-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3a7e545539453c5dfacd0828fae0fc39-chunk-003</data>
