<node id="doc_status">
  <data key="d0">doc_status</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The term `doc_status` refers to the status of a document, encompassing various aspects of its processing and management. It indicates the current state or progress of a document, which can include processing status, scanning progress, and the tracking of document processing. Specifically, `doc_status` serves as a means to monitor the progress of document processing and may involve handling cross-document deduplication and storing the content hash. This object-oriented representation of document status is integral to ensuring the integrity and efficiency of document management systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1df1634555d20a3b0378d0dc58979df0-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1df1634555d20a3b0378d0dc58979df0-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1df1634555d20a3b0378d0dc58979df0-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1df1634555d20a3b0378d0dc58979df0-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1df1634555d20a3b0378d0dc58979df0-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1df1634555d20a3b0378d0dc58979df0-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d37ce0e26a92a51f4827fa69633d38eb-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3a7e545539453c5dfacd0828fae0fc39-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3a7e545539453c5dfacd0828fae0fc39-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786009787</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
