<node id="LLM">
  <data key="d0">LLM</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">The LLM, or Large Language Model, is a type of artificial intelligence model designed to understand and generate human language. It plays a significant role in the configuration process and is utilized for tasks such as session title and keyword generation, particularly within platforms like Open WebUI. While primarily associated with the generation of textual content, LLMs also encompass a range of applications, including the analysis of table and equation objects, and the provision of LLM generation services by organizations. It's important to note that there is a distinction between LLMs and Low-level language models, with the latter being a type of model used in configuration systems. Additionally, there is a separate concept referred to as the Language Learning Model, which is distinct from the Large Language Model described here.&lt;SEP&gt;Language Learning Model&lt;SEP&gt;An acronym for "Language Learning Model," likely referring to a type of AI model</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8b4d4a34c28646786713dd9d097373d4-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-497eef1a84c2e1267fe9ef217a5f0106-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-497eef1a84c2e1267fe9ef217a5f0106-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-497eef1a84c2e1267fe9ef217a5f0106-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d37ce0e26a92a51f4827fa69633d38eb-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5ce3beac28f955cae00646a6f9e69a70-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a583d83915dae1536924c9149ccfaa0-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-640e5c41fd121c0003f70f439e8b3b48-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0f80f5fd1e3eb31ff80fc35d1fcf0198-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-753b54f11987ea184b7a7af0bb9e15ee-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786010992</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
