<node id="heading">
  <data key="d0">heading</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The heading is a fundamental element in document structure, serving as the top-most-level title or introductory text of a section or section within a document. It is a field that contains headings within the document, acting as the title or main heading of a section or block of content. In Markdown-like files, headings are used to locate content by their headings, and they also represent the current heading of a content line. The heading can be considered the title or introductory text of a chunk or a block, providing context and organization to the content it precedes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d37ce0e26a92a51f4827fa69633d38eb-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d37ce0e26a92a51f4827fa69633d38eb-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d37ce0e26a92a51f4827fa69633d38eb-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d37ce0e26a92a51f4827fa69633d38eb-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d37ce0e26a92a51f4827fa69633d38eb-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-832e2be61d469cc5f7dd74904c81d721-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-832e2be61d469cc5f7dd74904c81d721-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-832e2be61d469cc5f7dd74904c81d721-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-832e2be61d469cc5f7dd74904c81d721-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786008616</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
