<node id="format">
  <data key="d0">format</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The format of the content, currently fixed to `"plain_text"`.&lt;SEP&gt;The format of the table or content&lt;SEP&gt;A parameter that specifies the format of a table</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d37ce0e26a92a51f4827fa69633d38eb-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d37ce0e26a92a51f4827fa69633d38eb-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-832e2be61d469cc5f7dd74904c81d721-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-832e2be61d469cc5f7dd74904c81d721-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786008606</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="parent_headings">
  <data key="d0">parent_headings</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The term "parent_headings" refers to a structured array of strings that depict the hierarchical sequence of headings in a document. These headings represent the chain of ancestor titles that lead up to the current heading. The concept encompasses all the parent headings that are associated with the current heading, forming a hierarchy within the document. The parent_headings are calculated for each new heading, ensuring that the relationship between the heading and its preceding headings is maintained. This hierarchy not only includes the direct parent headings of a given heading but also the broader parent headings that are associated with the parent blocks of the heading. Furthermore, the parent_headings also establish the sequence of headings that serve as the ancestors of a specific block within the document. Additionally, the parent_headings form the chain of parent headings that lead up to any content line within the document, providing a comprehensive view of the document's heading structure.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d37ce0e26a92a51f4827fa69633d38eb-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d37ce0e26a92a51f4827fa69633d38eb-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-832e2be61d469cc5f7dd74904c81d721-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-832e2be61d469cc5f7dd74904c81d721-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-832e2be61d469cc5f7dd74904c81d721-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-832e2be61d469cc5f7dd74904c81d721-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-832e2be61d469cc5f7dd74904c81d721-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-832e2be61d469cc5f7dd74904c81d721-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786008613</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="level">
  <data key="d0">level</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The level of the heading in the document outline.&lt;SEP&gt;The level of a heading within the document&lt;SEP&gt;The heading level of a content line.</data>
