<node id="description">
  <data key="d0">description</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">The term "description" refers to a field used in various contexts to provide detailed information about entities and relationships. It encompasses a comprehensive analysis result, an equation, a drawing, and a table, among other objects. A description of an entity or relationship not only offers a basic definition but also provides context and attributes, elucidating the nature of the connection between source and target entities. This multifaceted field serves as a crucial tool for understanding the intricacies and characteristics of the entities and relationships it describes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d37ce0e26a92a51f4827fa69633d38eb-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d37ce0e26a92a51f4827fa69633d38eb-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d37ce0e26a92a51f4827fa69633d38eb-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-04e9a4e23946a2a3618f112c8e332247-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-adb132f201cb76c08df5059c6ef17d50-chunk-001</data>
