<node id="target_max">
  <data key="d0">target_max</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Target_max is a quantifiable threshold used to control the maximum size of chunks in various contexts, particularly within the handling and processing of text data. It represents the upper limit on the number of tokens or characters allowed in a single chunk of content. This method is crucial for managing the size of data segments to facilitate efficient merging and splitting processes, ensuring that the chunked content remains within optimal processing boundaries. The implementation of target_max as a limit helps to maintain the integrity and performance of data handling systems, providing a structured approach to managing data chunks that are used in applications requiring segmented processing.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-832e2be61d469cc5f7dd74904c81d721-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-832e2be61d469cc5f7dd74904c81d721-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-832e2be61d469cc5f7dd74904c81d721-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-832e2be61d469cc5f7dd74904c81d721-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-832e2be61d469cc5f7dd74904c81d721-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-832e2be61d469cc5f7dd74904c81d721-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-832e2be61d469cc5f7dd74904c81d721-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-832e2be61d469cc5f7dd74904c81d721-chunk-010</data>
