<edge source="LightRAG Server" target="supports">
  <data key="d7">10.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The LightRAG Server is a versatile server capable of operating in various modes and supporting a range of functionalities. It can run in Gunicorn + Uvicorn mode, as well as in Uvicorn mode alone. The server facilitates document management by allowing users to change parser routing and filename hints for new uploads by deleting and re-uploading documents. Additionally, it supports multimodal options with parsed sidecars and the VLM_PROCESS_ENABLE setting, which enhances its capabilities for handling diverse data types and processing requirements.

In terms of document processing, the LightRAG Server supports changing chunker settings for documents that are enqueued after server restarts. This feature ensures that the server can adapt to changes in document structure and processing needs. The server also offers flexibility in terms of language models and embeddings, supporting multiple LLM and Embedding backends to cater to different user preferences and requirements.

Configuration settings are made easier through the use of environment variables, which allows for efficient management of the server's operational parameters. Furthermore, the LightRAG Server enables reprocessing existing documents to run VLM analysis, providing users with the option to revisit and refine their analysis as needed. The server's support for VLM processing with the VLM_PROCESS_ENABLE setting further underscores its robustness and adaptability in handling complex data processing tasks.</data>
  <data key="d9">Embedding backends,Gunicorn + Uvicorn mode,Uvicorn mode,VLM processing with VLM_PROCESS_ENABLE setting,changing chunker settings for documents enqueued after server restarts,changing parser routing and filename hints for new uploads,environment variables for configuration,multimodal options with parsed sidecars and VLM_PROCESS_ENABLE,multiple LLM and Embedding backends for flexibility,reprocessing existing documents for VLM analysis</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-497eef1a84c2e1267fe9ef217a5f0106-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-497eef1a84c2e1267fe9ef217a5f0106-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d12">1786007569</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="LightRAG Server" target="uses">
  <data key="d7">12.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The LightRAG Server is a configuration-driven application that utilizes various tools and commands for its setup and operation. It requires environment variables for configuration, with the `.env` file serving as the primary source for these settings. Additionally, the server uses the `env.example` file as a reference for configuration options. For processing, the LightRAG Server employs LLM (Language Learning Model) and Embedding models. The server's development process involves the use of a virtual environment, and it utilizes the `make dev` command to set up the development environment.

For building front-end artifacts in the web UI project, the LightRAG Server uses the `bun run build` command. Dependencies for the web UI project are built using the `bun install` command. To install dependencies and tools, the server employs the `uv tool install` command for installations from PyPI and the `pip install` command for installations from source. For installations from source, the `git clone` command is used.

The LightRAG Server also follows a structured approach to development, utilizing the `git clone` command for source installations and the `pip install` command for source installations. It leverages the `bun install` command for building dependencies and the `bun run build` command for building front-end artifacts.</data>
  <data key="d9">.env,.env file for actual configuration settings,LLM and Embedding models,bun install command for building dependencies in the web UI project,bun run build command for building front-end artifacts in the web UI project,env.example file for configuration settings example,environment variables,git clone command for installation from source,make dev command for setting up the development environment,pip install command for installation from source,uv tool install command for installation from PyPI,virtual environment for development</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-497eef1a84c2e1267fe9ef217a5f0106-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-497eef1a84c2e1267fe9ef217a5f0106-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d12">1786007577</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
