<edge source="mineru-api" target="uses">
  <data key="d7">12.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The mineru-api container is an integral component designed to utilize various resources and configurations for its operation. It is configured and executed through the `docker compose` utility, utilizing a `compose.yaml` file for its setup. The container is equipped with specific features such as the `allow-public-http-client` flag, indicating its ability to handle public HTTP client requests. To ensure health checks, it incorporates the `health` concept, and it also leverages the `mineru-lightrag.json` file, the root directory, and the `curl` command. Furthermore, the container operates on port 8000 and uses `localhost` for its network interactions. The mineru-api container is capable of utilizing NVIDIA GPUs, particularly GPU 0, which suggests its support for high-performance computing tasks.</data>
  <data key="d9">8000,allow-public-http-client,api,compose.yaml,curl,docker compose,health,localhost,mineru-lightrag.json,nvidia,root</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-1df1634555d20a3b0378d0dc58979df0-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d12">1786006803</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="mineru-api" target="sets">
  <data key="d7">3.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The mineru-api container sets the MINERU_TOOLS_CONFIG_JSON environment variable&lt;SEP&gt;The mineru-api container sets the gpu-memory-utilization command-line option&lt;SEP&gt;The mineru-api container sets the MINERU_MODEL_SOURCE environment variable</data>
  <data key="d9">MINERU_MODEL_SOURCE,MINERU_TOOLS_CONFIG_JSON,gpu-memory-utilization</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-1df1634555d20a3b0378d0dc58979df0-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d12">1786006803</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
