<edge source="uses" target="embedding_func">
  <data key="d7">10.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The embedding_func is a function designed to handle various parameters and functionalities related to the creation and deployment of embeddings. It utilizes a partial function for wrapping the underlying function, which is essential for its operation. The embedding_func incorporates the embedding_dim parameter to define the dimension of the embeddings, ensuring that the resulting vectors have the desired level of detail and complexity.

In addition to the embedding_dim, the embedding_func makes use of the max_token_size parameter, which specifies the maximum token size allowed. This parameter helps in managing the input data for the embeddings, ensuring that only relevant and manageable pieces of text are processed.

The selection of the embedding model is facilitated by the model_name parameter, allowing users to choose the most suitable model for their specific needs. The embedding_func leverages the llama_index_embed.func for generating embeddings, which suggests a strong integration with the llama_index library.

For the embedding process, the embedding_func utilizes azure_openai_embed, indicating its compatibility with Azure OpenAI services. The deployment_name parameter is employed to specify the deployment name, which could be useful for identifying and managing different instances of the embedding_func.

Further, the embedding_func relies on the azure_endpoint parameter to set the endpoint URL for the API interactions, which is crucial for connecting to the appropriate resources. Additionally, the api_version parameter is used to specify the version of the API being interacted with, ensuring compatibility and consistency in the embedding process.

Authentication for the embedding_func is managed through the use of an API key, which provides access to the necessary services and data required for the embeddings to be created successfully.

In summary, the embedding_func is a versatile tool that encompasses various parameters and functionalities, including the use of partial functions, parameter-defined dimensions and token sizes, model selection, integration with specific libraries and services, and authentication mechanisms, all aimed at effectively generating embeddings.</data>
  <data key="d9">api_key for API key,api_version for API version,azure_endpoint for endpoint URL,azure_openai_embed for embedding,deployment_name for deployment name,embedding_dim for dimension,llama_index_embed.func for embedding,max_token_size for token size,model_name for model selection,partial for function wrapping</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-5ce3beac28f955cae00646a6f9e69a70-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d12">1786009152</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
