<edge source="contains" target="meta line example">
  <data key="d7">16.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The Meta line example is a structured data container that encapsulates various fields and files relevant to a document or digital asset. It includes the document_format field, which specifies the format of the document. Additionally, the meta line example contains the document_name field, which identifies the name of the document. The document_hash field is also present, serving as a unique identifier for the document.

Furthermore, the equation_file and drawing_file fields are part of the Meta line example, providing references to files containing mathematical equations and graphical representations, respectively. The split_option field indicates the option chosen for splitting the document, while the parse_engine field identifies the engine used for parsing the document.

Other fields within the Meta line example include the table_file, which points to a file containing tables, and the parse_time field, which records the time taken to parse the document. The asset_dir field refers to the directory containing the asset associated with the document, and the doc_title field provides the title of the document.

Additionally, the Meta line example includes the version field, indicating the version of the document, and the format field, which specifies the overall format of the document. The blocks field contains information about the document's structure, and the doc_id field serves as a unique identifier for the document.

The type field within the Meta line example classifies the document or asset into a specific category. The parse_engine and parse_time fields further provide insights into the document's processing and analysis. The Meta line example also includes the asset_dir, doc_title, version, format, blocks, and doc_id fields, which collectively provide a comprehensive overview of the document or digital asset.</data>
  <data key="d9">asset_dir field,blocks field,doc_id field,doc_title field,document_format field,document_hash field,document_name field,drawing_file field,equation_file field,format field,parse_engine field,parse_time field,split_option field,table_file field,type field,version field</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-d37ce0e26a92a51f4827fa69633d38eb-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d12">1786007740</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
