<edge source="New York" target="budget">
  <data key="d7">7.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The New York budget raised the minimum wage to $17 in New York City and $16 in the rest of the state by 2026.&lt;SEP&gt;The New York budget included provisions for eliminating the standard of "least restrictive" bail means.&lt;SEP&gt;The New York budget included provisions for banning gas stoves and furnaces in new buildings.&lt;SEP&gt;The New York budget raised the minimum wage from $15 in the city and $14.20 upstate.&lt;SEP&gt;The New York budget included provisions for cracking down on illicit pot shops.&lt;SEP&gt;The New York budget included provisions for raising the minimum wage.&lt;SEP&gt;The New York budget contained significant wins for New Yorkers.</data>
